    { "id": "note-journal", "page": "page-1", "x": 0, "y": -300, "w": 860, "text": "Journal — the chosen direction, filled out.\n\nNewsreader for content, Instrument Sans for labels and numerals. Paper ground, hairline rules instead of cards, one deep-green accent. Nothing is a container: hierarchy comes from type size and rule weight.\n\nThe ink theme is the same screen recoloured, not a second design — the app already ships light / dark / AMOLED, so 'Black' in Settings still needs drawing.\n\nTwo things here are not in the app yet: the 'write a line about today' field at the bottom of the list, and the linked-agent row in Settings showing coaching as an in-app toggle rather than only a notification channel." },
    { "id": "note-others", "page": "page-2", "x": 0, "y": -220, "w": 860, "text": "The four directions not taken, kept for reference. Each is one main screen and one detail screen, in English, with its own type voice: A Instrument Sans, B IBM Plex Sans, C Space Grotesk, E Figtree." }
  ],
